fell:
He tricked a mass of stars into his hair;
He filled his hands with stars, crying as he fell,
“A star’s a star although it burns in hell.”

And he bore the flask to the brightest spot,
Where the shadow of the hill fell clear;
And he turned the flask, and he looked at the flask,

felled:
Fate slew him, but he did not drop;
She felled -- he did not fall --
Impaled him on her fiercest stakes --
